id: decisions/014-gap-disclosure
title: "Name what the shape leaves out"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'gap-disclosure'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: gap-disclosure
axis_gloss: "whether what is missing is named in the record as a gap, or simply left out without trace"
poles:
  a: declared-lacuna
  b: silent-omission
split: leaning
draft_status: full
leverage: 18.5
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(22) x split_weight(0.7) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  When a record's serialized shape leaves out something its own prose calls a
  primitive, must the record name that gap as a lacuna, or may it just leave it
  out?

why_it_matters: >
  The written practice is to name gaps: timeouts are recorded as timeouts,
  private desires keep an id, the art contract publishes an open_lacunae list.
  The constitutional arena document drops regulation, repair, arena-level
  agents, five time fields, seven gravity contributors and the whole
  artificial_agent block from its data shape without a word. A bot building from
  section 14 inherits a shape that silently disagrees with sections 5 through 9;
  a child Yawn inherits whether omissions must be declared or may be quiet.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    12 judgments sit at declared-lacuna (4 authored) and 10 at silent-omission (0
    authored). The repository asserts both directions on this axis.
  attributed_to: JUDGMENTS.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Whether Dave holds section 14's shape to be normative over the prose (in which
    case the prose should shrink) or the prose to be the design (in which case the
    shape owes the gaps).

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      Anything a record's prose names as a primitive, input, or requirement and its
      serialized shape omits is listed in that record's lacunae: block with a
      reason. An unlisted omission is a defect, not a choice.
    cost: "An omitted_from_shape: list of roughly six entries in core/RELATIONSHIP_FIRST_AGENT_ARENA.yawn section 14; one sentence in core/lacuna.yawn."
    risk: "The arena document is status active, criticality constitutional; editing it needs Dave's hand, not a bot's."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "A new tests/arena-shape-coverage.test.mjs that parses the section 5-9 primitive lists and the section 14 shape, and asserts every prose primitive is either a shape field or a named entry in omitted_from_shape."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0065"
      - "J0321"
      - "J0371"
      - "J0401"
      - "J0441"
      - "J0610"
  - name: B
    description: >
      A serialized shape may omit prose-named primitives without note. The shape is
      normative; the prose is informative and may exceed it.
    cost: "A sentence in the arena document's frontmatter; nothing else changes."
    risk: "Readers of the prose and readers of the shape build different systems; the failure the prose predicts for omitting regulation goes unrecorded."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "None exists; B is honoured by the absence of a check."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0173"
      - "J0174"
      - "J0175"
      - "J0176"
      - "J0177"
      - "J0179"
  - name: C
    description: >
      Option A everywhere, except that core/RELATIONSHIP_FIRST_AGENT_ARENA.yawn and
      references/RELATIONSHIP_FIRST_RESEARCH_BRAID.yawn are grandfathered by name in
      a shrink-only ledger until Dave adds the omissions list.
    cost: "Two ledger entries; the same test as A with a GRANDFATHERED map."
    risk: "The ledger entry becomes permanent; the constitutional document stays the one place the rule does not hold."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Same test as A with a two-entry grandfather map and a size ceiling, following tests/epistemic-status-vocabulary.test.mjs."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0065"
      - "J0401"
      - "J0441"
      - "J0173"
      - "J0179"

recommendation:
  option_ref: A
  confidence: 0.75
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    All four authored judgments and both outcome-attached ones (J0065 why_added,
    J0401 a withheld-but-present desire) are on the declared-lacuna side; the repo
    already pays for naming gaps and has a lacuna primitive (core/lacuna.yawn) and
    lacunae: blocks in Dave's own models. Every silent omission is a reading of
    one file, which also has no proof block (GROUND_TRUTH FACT 3) and claims
    constitutional status with nineteen unchecked boxes (J0189). Writing six
    entries into section 14 is smaller than maintaining an exception for the
    constitution. C is the fallback if Dave will not edit the arena document now.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "core/RELATIONSHIP_FIRST_AGENT_ARENA.yawn section 14 carries an omitted_from_shape: list naming regulation, arena-level agents, repair, counterfactual_branch, accumulation, window, the seven dropped gravity contributors, and the artificial_agent block, each with a reason"
    - "A test in tests/ diffs the prose primitives against the shape and passes only when every gap is listed"
    - "core/lacuna.yawn states that a shape omission is a lacuna"

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A new schema drops a field its companion .yawn names as required and no
    lacunae entry or test failure appears.
  status: proposed

resolves:
  - "J0065"
  - "J0321"
  - "J0371"
  - "J0401"
  - "J0441"
  - "J0610"
  - "J0173"
  - "J0174"
  - "J0175"
  - "J0176"
  - "J0177"
  - "J0179"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
